      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    life_expectancy = 75\n    mean_years_school = 10\n    expected_years_school = 16\n    gni_per_capita = 35000\n\n    # Calculate normalized indices\n    life_expectancy_index = (life_expectancy - 20) / (85 - 20)\n    education_index = (\n        (mean_years_school / 15) + (expected_years_school / 18)\n    ) / 2\n    gni_index = (gni_per_capita - 100) / (75000 - 100)\n\n    # Calculate HDI using the geometric mean\n    hdi = (\n        life_expectancy_index * education_index * gni_index\n    ) ** (1 / 3)\n\n    # Return HDI rounded to three decimal places\n    return round(hdi, 3)\n```",
